  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\n\nThe H5 ridge will amplify over most of the central CONUS through at \nleast Friday. As the resultant 1000-500mb thicknesses expand, expect \ntemperatures to gain a few degrees each day. Thursday and Friday \nappear to be the warmest days of the upcoming week, with most areas \nseeing highs in the mid to upper 70s. A few H5 impulses may try to \nride the ridge and approach the area during that timeframe, but \nagain, little moisture return into the area will likely limit precip \ndevelopment. With this forecast update, NBM suggests a less than 10% \nchance for precip through early Friday so expect dry conditions to \nprevail.\n\nBy Friday into Saturday, model guidance hints at an H5 longwave \nejecting from the Intermountain West toward the Northern Plains. Lee \ncyclogenesis occurs with the sfc low tracking somewhere into the \nwestern Dakotas. A tight pressure gradient will set up across the \narea and lead to gusty southerly winds of 35 to 40 mph. Coupled with \nthis upcoming dry spell, could see some fire weather concerns \ndevelop in areas where fuels can cure fast enough. As the mid and \nlow level features approach the area, should see our next chance for \nrain by early Saturday morning (20 to 40%).",
